1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,194
How does a repository reach your service?

2
00:00:02,374 --> 00:00:04,680
Configured scanning finds annotated classes

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,163
and registers bean definitions.

4
00:00:07,383 --> 00:00:10,180
A single constructor needs a repository.

5
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:12,751
Spring resolves that parameter by type.

6
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:15,120
Spring creates the repository,

7
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,220
then passes its reference

8
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:18,222
into the service constructor.

9
00:00:18,442 --> 00:00:19,620
Our Java run confirms

10
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,900
the same repository bean.

11
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,200
Only then does the application

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,934
use the service.

13
00:00:25,154 --> 00:00:27,820
Scan, register, resolve, inject, then use.

14
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,760
Spring supplies dependencies;

15
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,209
your service doesn’t construct them.

16
00:00:34,209 --> 00:00:35,300
Thanks for watching.

